+/*
+ * Patch 0361: an RX ring and TX batches. Before, one TRB per direction was
+ * in flight and ud_thread re-armed it only on its next 1 ms poll: at most one
+ * frame per poll and direction (measured 1.1-1.2 MB/s both ways at high
+ * speed). Now UD_RXN receive TRBs form a ring (link TRB at the end) that the
+ * controller fills without us, and up to UD_TXB queued frames go out in one
+ * transfer (one TRB per frame, LST + IOC on the last). DMA is not cache
+ * coherent: an RX TRB is armed again only when all 4 TRBs of its 64-byte
+ * cache line are done, so a cache clean never overwrites a TRB the controller
+ * is writing back. Boot-arg negroniusb_ring=0: the old one-TRB paths.
